Meaning Banks — Semantic Banking Architecture

> **Canonical principle:** Do not merely store definitions; store what lets meaning be reconstructed.
> 
> **Checksum:** Did the word cross, or did the meaning cross?

Meaning Banks are a Pantheon semantic-logistics capability for preserving, comparing, transferring, and reconstituting meaning without pretending a term has one timeless definition.

A term is a semantic token whose value is backed by a meaning reserve: usage, context, relations, examples, etymology, stories, evidence, competing interpretations, and the deltas connecting one state of meaning to another.

The bank metaphor is an interface. The mechanism underneath it is:

TRACE → PROVENANCE → RELATION → DELTA → RECONSTRUCTION → TASK-SPECIFIC PROJECTION

Placement

```text
SEMANTIC QUARRY
    discover / extract
          ↓
MEANING BANKS
    accounts / deposits / reserves / deltas / exchange routes
          ↓
STRATIGRAPHY / STRATA
    history / translation / loss audit
          ↓
GOLDEN HORDE / SEMANTIC MUSTER
    retrieve what the objective needs
          ↓
FORMATION / ACTION
          ↓
AFTERGLOW + DELTA
          ↘ useful semantic change returns to the bank
```

Core objects

• MeaningAccount — addressable term/concept ledger; not a fixed definition.
• MeaningDeposit — a meaning trace with context, epistemic status, confidence, provenance, and reconstruction cues.
• MeaningReserve — a candidate invariant supported by multiple traces.
• SemanticDelta — a directed arrow describing what changed between deposits.
• ExchangeRoute — a mapping across language/domain/community boundaries with explicit losses and gains.
• MeaningPacket — a temporary, task-specific projection assembled from the reserve.

Operations

DEPOSIT • RESERVE • DELTA • RETRIEVE • PRISM • EXCHANGE • TRANSDICT • AUDIT • PRESSURE • PACKET • PREFLIGHT

Trans-dict-ion

Trans-dict-ion gets a relational pattern to say itself across a boundary:

meaning₁ → carrier → crossing → reconstruction → meaning₂

A route records what survived, what was lost, and what new affordances appeared.

Semantic banking interfaces

These are inspection metaphors, not literal economic laws:

• semantic inflation — one term spreads across many weakly distinguished senses.
• semantic debasement — a prestigious label remains while properties that backed it are removed.
• semantic counterfeiting — surface resemblance borrows another concept’s authority without carrying its reserve.
• semantic arbitrage — differences between communities’ interpretations are exploited.
• semantic reserve — the contexts, evidence, relations, and traces backing a term.
• meaning vault — durable provenance-preserving storage supporting reconstruction rather than frozen definitions.

Emergent runtime capability

pantheon_adapter.py adds semantic preflight before normal routing:

```text
PERCEIVE
  ↓
STRUCTURE
  ↓
SEMANTIC PREFLIGHT
  ├─ continue
  ├─ use_packet
  ├─ prism
  └─ audit
  ↓
UPDATE STATE / ROUTE / MUSTER
  ...
AFTERGLOW
  ↓
SEMANTIC DELTA DEPOSIT
```

Routing law:

• continue — no useful banked material.
• use_packet — a context-relevant semantic projection is available.
• prism — the surface is genuinely overloaded or multiple readings remain competitive.
• audit — provenance/evidence pressure deserves inspection.

This makes the bank a live interface, not a passive archive.

Minimal example

```python
from meaning_bank import MeaningBank

bank = MeaningBank("bank.json")

a = bank.deposit(
    term="acting",
    sense="performing or pretending a role",
    language="en",
    context="movie / theater",
    domain="performance",
    epistemic_status="attested",
    confidence=0.95,
    provenance=["corpus:acting-performance"],
)

b = bank.deposit(
    term="acting",
    sense="taking action; doing rather than remaining passive",
    language="en",
    context="agency / decision",
    domain="agency",
    epistemic_status="attested",
    confidence=0.95,
    provenance=["corpus:acting-agency"],
)

bank.delta(
    source_id=a.id,
    target_id=b.id,
    relation="polysemy_bridge",
    description="The same surface form moves from role-performance to real-world action.",
    changed_dimensions=["frame", "agency"],
    confidence=0.9,
)

packet = bank.packet(
    "acting",
    language="en",
    context="pretending becomes action",
    domain="agency",
)
```

Design law

A Meaning Bank does not own meaning. It keeps the ledger open enough that meaning cannot change invisibly.